title: $:/changenotes/5.5.0/getattribute-operator
description: New getattribute operator for reading attributes of widget, element and macro invocations
release: 5.5.0
tags: $:/tags/ChangeNote
change-type: feature
change-category: filters

The new [[getattribute Operator]] parses each input title as inline ~WikiText and returns the value of a named attribute of the widget, HTML element or macro invocation that it consists of.

It removes the need for regular expressions when picking apart an invocation, and recognises all of the equivalent ways of writing one, so that `<<colour foreground>>`, `<<colour name:foreground>>` and `<$transclude $variable="colour" name="foreground"/>` are all handled by `getattribute[name],[0]`.

The $:/PaletteEditor uses it to resolve palette entries that are defined in terms of another entry.
